            <ArticleTitle>The management of angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Modern treatment has improved the outlook for patients with angina pectoris. Full clinical assessment and hospital referral is justified for many patients in order to determine whether they should be considered for bypass surgery or balloon angioplasty, even if symptoms are not disabling. An enthusiastic approach to risk factor modification is an important element of medical treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
